{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018NJoUu7mn6WsUdDzEwydAe","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fb6b059-d3b5-4b61-b723-cd48424c37bd","uuid":"b04f27fa-910d-43f3-9182-f9b9b215515d","timestamp":"2026-06-11T01:58:52.371Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **sos_1**: The attack trigger's \"target\" is chosen at trigger *resolution*","newString":"- **sos_97 / engine**: Loyalty-ability targets — TODO said to read\n  `self.chosen_targets` \"set by the engine from the activation's targets\",\n  but no such path existed. Added `LoyaltyAbilityInstance.targets`\n  (default None) and a resolve-time write of `source.chosen_targets` in\n  `_activate_loyalty_ability` — additive, mirrors `_resolve_spell`, and\n  existing FDN walkers (which read `_resolve_target`) are unaffected.\n- **sos_97 / engine**: `GameState.rng` (seedable `random.Random`) added for\n  deterministic coin flips; `skip_turns` honored in `advance_phase`'s\n  turn-wrap loop (a skipped player's would-be turn is forfeited, one skip\n  consumed per would-be turn; `turn_number` does not advance for skipped\n  turns).\n- **sos_97**: Surveil 2 keeps surviving cards in their existing order (no\n  reorder prompt — `Player` has no order-choice API beyond damage\n  assignment); binning is asked top-down via yes/no per card. The −1\n  discard is each player's own choice (`choose_card`), falling back to the\n  last card if the scripted choice is invalid.\n- **sos_1**: The attack trigger's \"target\" is chosen at trigger *resolution*","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\n- **E1**: Fired `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in `cast_spell_free` as well as\n  `cast_spell` — TODO only named `cast_spell`, but per rule 601.2 casting\n  without paying the mana cost is still casting, so cast triggers (e.g.\n  Casualty on sos_226) must see free casts too. Copies made by `copy_spell`\n  still correctly do not fire it (copies are not cast). Populated the event's\n  `player` field alongside `controller` (same value) since existing FDN code\n  (fdn_248) reads `event.player or event.controller`.\n- **sos_1 / engine**: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` existed but was never fired (Etali\n  fdn_194 registers for it too). Fired it once per declared attacker at the end\n  of `declare_attackers_step` (rule 508.1m) — the single chokepoint both\n  `run_turn` and the `declare_attackers` test helper pass through.\n- **sos_1 / engine**: `move_to_zone` only consulted replacement effects for\n  battlefield departures, so \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n  exile it instead\" could never apply to a resolving spell. Added\n  `SpellPutIntoGraveyardReplacementEvent` and made `_resolve_spell` pass it;\n  `move_to_zone` now also applies replacements when the source zone is STACK.\n  Existing callers are unaffected (they pass replacement events only for\n  battlefield moves). Limitation: a spell countered via the card-local\n  `_counter_spell` path (fdn_48 mirror) bypasses `move_to_zone`, so\n  exile-instead does not apply there — acceptable corner case.\n- **sos_257 / engine**: Restricted mana is a single-purpose parallel pool in\n  `ManaPool` (`add_restricted` / `get_restricted`); `can_pay`/`pay` gained an\n  optional `spell=` kwarg (passed by `cast_spell`) and merge restricted mana\n  only when the spell is an instant/sorcery, consuming restricted mana before\n  unrestricted of the same type. One restriction kind only — deliberately not\n  a general restriction system.\n- **sos_257**: Animation mutates in place and updates `_original_card_types`\n  so `EffectManager.apply_all`'s reset cycle doesn't strip the Creature type\n  (the printed ability has no duration). `_reset_characteristics` mirrors\n  Creature's so the +1/+0 pump (a layer-7c `ContinuousEffect`, EOT duration)\n  recalculates idempotently and sweeps at cleanup. Limitations (commented):\n  a land played the same turn really has summoning sickness (not tracked);\n  if the animated land leaves the battlefield the Creature type stays baked\n  into the card object (animation-wears-off-on-zone-change not modeled).\n- **sos_257 tests**: There is no `ActivateAbility(card, index)` helper in\n  `test_utils`; abilities are driven by printed index via\n  `get_*_abilities()[index]` wrapped in `ActivatedAbilityInstance` and passed\n  through `engine.abilities.activate_ability` (the engine's real activation\n  entry point), resolving non-mana abilities through `priority_loop`.\n- **sos_57**: \"Your next main phase\" is approximated as your next *precombat*\n  main (E2 fires only there). If Mana Sculpt resolves during your own\n  precombat main, the mana arrives at your next turn's precombat main instead\n  of this turn's postcombat main — accepted simplification per TODO. The\n  Wizard check happens when the delayed trigger fires (per TODO), not at\n  resolution; the trigger is one-shot either way. \"Mana spent\" reads the new\n  `card.mana_spent` recorded at cast time (0 for free casts; X not supported\n  by the engine's cost model).\n- **sos_120**: The Paradigm copy uses `copy_spell` per TODO, so it does not\n  fire cast triggers — the glossary's \"cast a copy\" is modeled as a stack\n  copy (consistent with how copies work everywhere else in this engine).\n  \"After you first resolve a spell with this name\" is tracked once per\n  player per card name via `ctrl._paradigm_armed`; the recurring trigger's\n  condition also requires the exiled Capstone to still be in exile. The\n  copy's own resolution re-runs the exile/cast clauses but cannot re-arm\n  Paradigm and exiles nothing (a copy exists in no zone).\n- **sos_13**: Rule 722.3c — the prepared copy is a real Swords to Plowshares\n  cast for its normal {W} cost (TODO had said free; rulebook wins). Exposed\n  as a public `cast_prepared_copy(game)` method (no engine seam exists for\n  \"may cast\" special permissions); it pays {W}, casts the copy from exile\n  through the real stack, and unprepares on cast. The copy is flagged\n  `is_token` so the existing SBA sweeps it after resolution (\"a copy ceases\n  to exist\"). Simplification vs 722.3c: the copy is created at election time\n  rather than sitting in exile from the moment of preparing — avoids\n  stale-copy cleanup when the creature leaves or unprepares.\n- **sos_13**: ETB effect implemented in `on_resolve` (FDN convention) because\n  the engine fires the ETB event before the entering permanent's\n  `register_triggers` runs — a self-ETB trigger can never see its own entry.\n  Count check adds 1 for the creature itself (still on the stack during\n  `on_resolve`). Limitation: entering untaxed (reanimation) skips the ETB,\n  same as every FDN reference creature.\n- **sos_201**: Miracle's \"first card you drew this turn\" is tracked by a\n  turn-stamped counter on the Lorehold instance (the engine's\n  `cards_drawn_this_turn` never resets). Limitation: the counter starts when\n  Lorehold's triggers register, so draws made earlier in the same turn it\n  entered are not counted. Miracle pays {2} from the pool, then uses the\n  free-cast stack path (and stamps `mana_spent = 2`); the can_pay check\n  happens before the \"may\" prompt, so an unpayable miracle never prompts.\n- **sos_1**: The attack trigger's \"target\" is chosen at trigger *resolution*\n  (the engine's trigger system has no targeting at announce time); with exactly\n  one legal candidate it is auto-selected per TODO, otherwise `choose_card`\n  answers with the card or `None` to decline the \"may\".\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":77,"oldLines":6,"newStart":77,"newLines":22,"lines":["   entered are not counted. Miracle pays {2} from the pool, then uses the","   free-cast stack path (and stamps `mana_spent = 2`); the can_pay check","   happens before the \"may\" prompt, so an unpayable miracle never prompts.","+- **sos_97 / engine**: Loyalty-ability targets — TODO said to read","+  `self.chosen_targets` \"set by the engine from the activation's targets\",","+  but no such path existed. Added `LoyaltyAbilityInstance.targets`","+  (default None) and a resolve-time write of `source.chosen_targets` in","+  `_activate_loyalty_ability` — additive, mirrors `_resolve_spell`, and","+  existing FDN walkers (which read `_resolve_target`) are unaffected.","+- **sos_97 / engine**: `GameState.rng` (seedable `random.Random`) added for","+  deterministic coin flips; `skip_turns` honored in `advance_phase`'s","+  turn-wrap loop (a skipped player's would-be turn is forfeited, one skip","+  consumed per would-be turn; `turn_number` does not advance for skipped","+  turns).","+- **sos_97**: Surveil 2 keeps surviving cards in their existing order (no","+  reorder prompt — `Player` has no order-choice API beyond damage","+  assignment); binning is asked top-down via yes/no per card. The −1","+  discard is each player's own choice (`choose_card`), falling back to the","+  last card if the scripted choice is invalid."," - **sos_1**: The attack trigger's \"target\" is chosen at trigger *resolution*","   (the engine's trigger system has no targeting at announce time); with exactly","   one legal candidate it is auto-selected per TODO, otherwise `choose_card`"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
